  "rules": "DECK. {deck_size} cards in {suits} suits: Ruins, Idols, Deep, Stars, Shore. Each suit has {cards_per_suit} cards: {plain_cards_per_suit} plain and {madness_cards_per_suit} with a madness icon (written e.g. 'Deep*').\n\nSTRUCTURE. The game has {total_rounds} rounds in {tides} tides of {rounds_per_tide} rounds each: rounds 1-5 are tide 1, rounds 6-10 tide 2, rounds 11-15 tide 3. Each player has a score (starting at {starting_score}) and a madness total (starting at {starting_madness}).\n\nSTART OF EACH TIDE (rounds 1, 6, 11). All 30 cards are shuffled, minus any cards currently retained by players. Each player is dealt a private hand of {hand_size}. The rest are unused this tide. Each player sees only their own hand. At the same moment as their first pick, each player secretly chooses one suit as their Obsession for this tide. It is hidden from the opponent until the tide is scored.\n\nEACH ROUND. Both players simultaneously choose one card from the hand they currently hold and place it face down in their tableau for this tide. Then the two players swap their remaining hands. Hands therefore go 5, 4, 3, 2, 1 cards, and the pick in the fifth round of a tide is forced (you are offered only the one remaining card). A player always knows the cards they themselves drafted and the hands they saw.\n\nEND OF EACH TIDE (rounds 5, 10, 15), in order:\n1. Reveal. Both tableaus and both Obsessions are revealed. A player's tide tableau is the 5 cards drafted this tide plus all cards they have retained from earlier tides.\n2. Madness. Each player counts madness icons in their tide tableau (retained cards count every tide they are in) and adds that number to their madness total.\n3. Set points. For each suit, count the cards of that suit in the tableau: 0 cards = {set_points_0} points, 1 = {set_points_1}, 2 = {set_points_2}, 3 = {set_points_3}, 4 or more = {set_points_4_or_more}. Points for the player's Obsession suit are multiplied by {obsession_multiplier} (e.g. 3 cards score 12); other suits score normally.\n4. Extra points. Add +{points_per_madness_card} point per madness card in the tableau. Add +{diversity_bonus} points if the tableau contains at least {diversity_suits_needed} different suits; with fewer suits, no bonus.\n5. Madness bonus. The player with strictly more madness icons in their tide tableau privately chooses one: gain {madness_bonus_points} points (gain_4_points), or reduce their madness total by {madness_bonus_reduction} (reduce_madness_1). If the counts are equal, nobody gets the bonus and nobody is asked.\n6. Madness check. If a player's madness total is {madness_loss_threshold} or more, the game ends immediately and that player loses. If both are at {madness_loss_threshold} or more, the one with the higher madness total loses. If they are equal, the game is a draw. If nobody is at {madness_loss_threshold} or more, play continues.\n7. Retain (tides 1 and 2 only). Each player simultaneously chooses one card drafted this tide to retain permanently. It stays face up beside them and is part of every later tide tableau (for set points, madness icons, the per-madness-card point and the suit bonus). All other drafted cards return to the deck. After tide 3 no card is retained.\n\nEND OF GAME. A player loses immediately if their madness total reaches {madness_loss_threshold} or more at a tide's madness check. If both reach it, the higher madness total loses, and equal totals are a draw. Otherwise, after tide 3 the higher score wins. If scores are tied, the lower madness total wins. If that is also tied, the game is a draw.",
